  "body": "With array-method optimizations enabled, filtering an already modified draft visits elements appended by the predicate. Reading source.length on every iteration differs from Array.prototype.filter, which captures the initial length, and an appending predicate can keep extending the loop.\n\nCapture the length before invoking the predicate. The regression compares plugin-enabled and regular behavior with auto-freezing enabled and disabled, including final draft and base contents.\n\nValidation (Node.js 24.15.0, Windows): The two plugin-enabled regressions fail before the fix. Source suite: 4,015 passing, 8 skipped. npm run build passes. Built-bundle suite: 3,464 passing, 8 skipped.\n\nAI assistance: this contribution was prepared with OpenAI Codex; the change and regression results were reviewed before submission.\n",
